{"reasoning": "The user is asking a multi-hop question: 1) Identify the war in which 'The Things They Carried' is set. 2) Determine the country where the film 'Grievous Bodily Harm' was later released (or originated). 3) Find out when conscription was introduced by that specific country.\n\nStep 1: The Things They Carried is set during the Vietnam War (Passage 0).\nStep 2: Grievous Bodily Harm is a 1988 Australian crime film (Passage 6). This identifies Australia as the relevant country.\nStep 3: I need to find when conscription was introduced in Australia. Passage 9 details this history.", "finding": "The Things They Carried is set during the Vietnam War (Passage 0).\nGrievous Bodily Harm is an Australian crime film (Passage 6). The relevant country is Australia.\nIn Australia, a form of conscription for boys from 12 to 14 years of age and for youths of 18 to 20 years of age was introduced in the Defence Act 1909 (Passage 9). Furthermore, compulsory military training for all males aged between 12 and 26 started on 1 January 1911 (Passage 9).", "answer": "a form of conscription for boys from 12 to 14 years of age and for youths of 18 to 20 years of age was introduced in the Defence Act 1909", "next_query": null}
