{"reasoning": "The user is asking for the president of the group that Kim Un-yong is a member of. I need to first identify what groups or organizations Kim Un-yong was a member of, and then find the president of one of those groups.\n\nSearching the documents reveals information about 'Kim Un-yong' in Passage 6.\nPassage 6 states that Kim Un-yong was: \n1. vice-president of the International Olympic Committee (IOC).\n2. founding member of the WTF executive board.\n3. elected president of the Korean Taekwondo Association on 23 January 1971.\n4. first president of the World Taekwondo Federation in 1973.\n5. President of the Korean Olympic Committee, President of the 2002 Pusan Asian Games Organization Committee, President of the Korea Taekwondo Association, President of World Taekwondo Headquarters (Kukkiwon), and internationally, he was the President of GAISF, Executive Board Member of the IOC, Chairman of the IOC Radio and Television Commission, and President of the World Taekwondo Federation.\n\nI have multiple groups. I will check which group's president is mentioned or who presided over it when Kim Un-yong held a role.\n\n*   **IOC:** Kim Un-yong was an Executive Board Member. Passage 3 lists various IOC presidents (Vikelas, de Coubertin, Baillet-Latour, Edström, Brundage, Killanin, Samaranch, Rogge, Bach). \n*   **WTF/World Taekwondo Federation:** He was the first president and later retired from the WTF presidency in 2004. The document mentions he was succeeded by Chungwon Choue.\n\nSince Kim Un-yong *was* President of the World Taekwondo Federation (WTF), I will check if there is a clear answer about who presided over his main groups during or after his involvement, or if one role is more significant. \n\nThe question asks for 'the' president, implying one specific group. Since he held multiple leadership roles, I need to see if the documents specify which group he belongs to implicitly or explicitly in relation to a current/specific president.\n\nLet's look at his relationship with the IOC (Passage 6: Executive Board Member of the IOC) and check for its current leader. Passage 3 lists past presidents, but not necessarily the *current* one if the document is historical.\n\nI will search for the president of the International Olympic Committee or World Taekwondo Federation.", "finding": "Kim Un-yong was a founding member/executive board member of the WTF and held numerous positions including President of the World Taekwondo Federation, President of the Korean Taekwondo Association, and Executive Board Member of the IOC. Passage 6 states he retired from the WTF presidency in 2004, being succeeded by Chungwon Choue. Passage 3 lists several past Presidents of the IOC: Demetrius Vikelas, Pierre, Baron de Coubertin, Henri, Comte de Baillet-Latour, Sigfrid Edström, Avery Brundage, Lord Killanin, Juan Antonio Samaranch, Jacques Count Rogge, and Thomas Bach.", "answer": null, "next_query": "president of the International Olympic Committee today or Chungwon Choue successor to World Taekwondo Federation"}
