{"reasoning": "The user is asking a multi-hop question: 'Along with the Closer performer, what notable pop artist started out his career on adult contemporary radio?'\n\nStep 1: Identify the 'Closer performer'. Passage 6 identifies Josh Groban as the vocalist for the album 'Closer'. So, the closer performer is Josh Groban.\n\nStep 2: Determine which notable pop artists started their career on Adult Contemporary (AC) radio. I need to search the documents for artists who fit this description.\n\nPassage 1 mentions several artists in AC history:\n- Early roots (1960s): Frank Sinatra, Doris Day, Johnny Mathis, Connie Francis, Nat King Cole, Perry Como.\n- After 1965: Roger Miller, Barbra Streisand, Bobby Vinton.\n- 1970s: Carole King, Cat Stevens, James Taylor, Bread, The Carpenters, Anne Murray, John Denver, Barry Manilow, Diana Ross, Carly Simon, Janis Ian, Elvis Presley, Linda Ronstadt, Elton John, Rod Stewart, Billy Joel. (Note: These were played on AC, not necessarily *started* their careers there).\n- 1980s: Barbra Streisand, the Carpenters, Dionne Warwick, Barry Manilow, John Denver, Olivia Newton-John, Richard Marx, Michael Jackson, Bonnie Tyler, George Michael, Phil Collins, Laura Branigan, Journey. (Again, these are artists associated with AC).\n\nPassage 6 mentions Josh Groban's song \"You Raise Me Up\" charted at No. 73 on the Billboard Hot 100 and #1 on the Adult Contemporary chart.\n\nStep 3: Re-evaluate based on the phrasing 'started out his career on adult contemporary radio'. The provided documents heavily detail artists who *were* played on AC radio, but do not explicitly state which ones *began their careers* exclusively or primarily on that format. However, the question asks for an artist *along with* the Closer performer (Josh Groban).\n\nThe phrasing implies a pair of performers.\n\nLet's look closely at Passage 1 again regarding early AC artists:\n\"Initially, the vocalists consisted of artists such as Frank Sinatra, Doris Day, Johnny Mathis, Connie Francis, Nat King Cole, Perry Como, and others.\"\nThese names are strong candidates for starting careers on easy listening/AC radio in the 1960s roots mentioned.\n\nSince Josh Groban is the 'Closer performer' (from Passage 6), I need another artist who fits the description. None of the provided text directly links an artist to *starting* their career specifically on AC, but it does list prominent artists associated with early AC radio play.\n\nI will check if any names overlap or if there is a direct pairing mentioned. The question structure suggests two notable pop artists are being compared/listed together.\n\nSince the documents do not provide definitive proof of which listed artist *started* their career on AC, and Josh Groban is established as 'The Closer performer', I must search for another name that fits the criteria from the provided text. \n\nGiven the available evidence, I cannot definitively identify a second artist who started his career *on* adult contemporary radio alongside Josh Groban based solely on these passages.", "finding": "Josh Groban is identified as the vocalist of the album 'Closer' (Passage 6). Passage 1 lists several artists whose music was played on AC radio in its history, including Frank Sinatra, Doris Day, Johnny Mathis, Connie Francis, Nat King Cole, and Perry Como from the early roots period.", "answer": null, "next_query": "Which notable pop artist started his career on adult contemporary radio alongside Josh Groban?"}
